        "original_id": "e9fdfd48-6b2b-52ee-97a9-bd8c4cf2d997",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Georg F. von Tiesenhausen, Wernher von Braun\n- Events: Operation Paperclip, World War II\n- Organizations: Joint Intelligence Objectives Agency\n- Roles: rocket scientists, engineers, technicians\n- Topics: German-American scientists, Nazi Party membership\n\nFacts:\n- Georg F. von Tiesenhausen was born on May 18, 1914.\n- Georg F. von Tiesenhausen is a retired German-American rocket scientist.\n- At the end of World War II, Operation Paperclip was a secret program of the Joint Intelligence Objectives Agency.\n- In post-Nazi Germany, Operation Paperclip recruited more than 1,600 German scientists, engineers, and technicians for U.S. government employment.\n- Operation Paperclip included Wernher von Braun and his V-2 rocket team among the recruits taken to the United States.\n- Many Operation Paperclip recruits were members of the Nazi Party, and some were Nazi Party leaders.",
